@event picture_lyra
# en: Unbearable
title [447d58] = 受不了
# en: You bring Lyra toast after practice, because she can't make it, and set it down without a word, because she won't ask. She looks at it, and at you. "You know about the toast," she says. "And my mother. And the Trials, and the letter, and the flourish." A pause. "You know everything. It's unbearable." She takes a slice anyway.
text [b249fa] = 练习结束后，你给莱拉送去吐司，因为她不会做；你一言不发地放下，因为她不会开口要。她看看吐司，又看看你。“你知道吐司的事，”她说，“还有我母亲。还有冬季考核，那封信，那个起手式。”停顿了一下。“你什么都知道。真让人受不了。”她还是拿起了一片。
# en: A duelling hall after dark, one student sitting on the floor against the wall, another handing her a plate of slightly burnt toast.
scene [d6684b] = 入夜后的决斗厅，一个学生靠墙坐在地上，另一个递给她一盘有点烤焦的吐司。
# en: "I'd like to know more."
opt.left.label [0aefe3] = “我还想知道更多。”
# en: "There isn't any more," she says, and then, after a long time, tells you one more thing: the name of her grandmother's horse. It doesn't matter at all. It's the first thing she has ever told you that she didn't have to.
opt.left.say.1 [7fe72b] = “没有更多了，”她说，然后过了很久，又告诉了你一件事：她祖母那匹马的名字。这根本无关紧要。这是她第一次告诉你一件她没必要说的事。
# en: "I'll forget half of it, if you like."
opt.right.label [c5e014] = “你愿意的话，我忘掉一半。”
# en: "Don't you dare," she says, too quickly, and then goes red. She eats the toast. It's burnt. She says it's adequate, which from Lyra is a bouquet, and doesn't let you leave until it's finished.
opt.right.say.1 [6755df] = “你敢，”她说得太快，随即红了脸。她吃了吐司。烤焦了。她说还过得去，这话从莱拉嘴里说出来就是一束花，而且在你吃完之前不许你走。

@event picture_corvin
# en: No Jokes
title [08a66e] = 不开玩笑
# en: Up on the parapet, Corvin shuffles his grandfather's deck and doesn't deal. "You know about the trolls," he says. "And my brother. And the warning. And the Sundays." He laughs, but only a little. "Nobody knows all of it, saint. I don't usually let anyone have more than two." The jokes have stopped. So has he.
text [1e8301] = 在矮墙上，科尔文洗着他祖父的那副牌，却不发。“你知道巨魔的事，”他说，“还有我哥哥。还有最后警告。还有星期天。”他笑了，但只笑了一点点。“没人知道全部，圣人。我通常只让人知道两件。”玩笑停了。他也停了。
# en: A gargoyle passage at night, two students sitting on the parapet, one shuffling a worn old deck of cards very slowly.
scene [94ea19] = 夜里的石像鬼通道，两个学生坐在矮墙上，其中一个非常缓慢地洗着一副旧牌。
# en: Tell him something of yours
opt.left.label [cd3f79] = 告诉他一件你自己的事
# en: You tell him the thing you don't tell anyone. He listens, the way his grandfather probably did, and then deals you a hand. "Now we're even," he says. "Don't you dare tell anyone I said something nice." You don't.
opt.left.say.1 [713d18] = 你告诉了他那件你从不告诉任何人的事。他听着，大概就像他祖父当年那样听着，然后给你发了一手牌。“现在扯平了，”他说，“敢告诉别人我说了好话，你就完了。”你没说。
# en: Let him deal, and say nothing
opt.right.label [838085] = 让他发牌，什么也不说
# en: You don't say anything, which turns out to be right. He deals. You play badly, and he lets you win once, which you both pretend not to notice. Somewhere around midnight he starts joking again, and it sounds different.
opt.right.say.1 [e129f7] = 你什么也没说，结果这样才对。他发了牌。你打得很差，他让你赢了一把，你们俩都假装没注意到。快到午夜时，他又开始开玩笑了，听起来却不一样了。

@event picture_tobias
# en: A Saying for It
title [b205e7] = 有句老话
# en: Repotting seedlings, Tobias goes quiet for so long that Gerald, on his shelf, stops screaming to look. "You know about my ma, and the blight, and the broom," he says. "And about after. I haven't told anyone about after." He wipes his hands on his apron. "Back home there's a saying for someone who knows you like that. I'll get it wrong."
text [f88488] = 给秧苗换盆的时候，托拜厄斯沉默了很久，久到架子上的杰拉德都停下尖叫来看他。“你知道我娘的事，还有枯萎病，还有那把扫帚，”他说，“还有以后的事。以后的事我谁都没告诉过。”他在围裙上擦了擦手。“老家有句话，说的就是像你这样了解一个人的人。我会说错的。”
# en: A greenhouse in the evening, two students repotting seedlings side by side, a small mandrake in a knitted hat watching from a shelf.
scene [c48a01] = 傍晚的温室里，两个学生并肩给秧苗换盆，一株戴着针织帽的小曼德拉草在架子上看着。
# en: Ask him to say it anyway
opt.left.label [4d16c0] = 请他照样说出来
# en: He says it, and gets it wrong, and then tells you the long version, which is about a goat. By the end you're both laughing so hard you knock over a tray of seedlings. They don't seem to mind. Gerald does.
opt.left.say.1 [220ca0] = 他说了，说错了，然后又讲了个长版本，是关于一头山羊的。讲到最后，你们俩笑得打翻了一盘秧苗。秧苗似乎不介意。杰拉德介意。
# en: Promise to help, whatever he decides
opt.right.label [f0e79e] = 无论他怎么决定，都答应帮他
# en: He looks at you for a long moment, and then laughs from the belly, the way he does, and apologises for laughing, the way he does. "That's the saying," he says. "Near enough." He gives you the best seedling to keep.
opt.right.say.1 [0de78a] = 他看了你好一会儿，然后像他平常那样从肚子里笑出来，又像他平常那样为笑而道歉。“就是这句话，”他说，“差不多。”他把最好的一株秧苗送给了你。

@event picture_seraphine
# en: Forty-One Todays
title [09d448] = 四十一个今天
# en: Seraphine gives you a little calendar she has stitched herself. Forty-one of its days have a tiny star on them. "The days you told me what today was," she says. "I slip, and you always know. And you know the rest: my mother, the lake, what gets too loud." She frowns, the way she does at a future. "Nobody's ever kept me in today before. I wanted you to have the count."
text [3943ec] = 塞拉芬送给你一本她亲手缝的小日历。上面有四十一天画着一颗小小的星。“这些是你告诉我今天是哪天的日子，”她说，“我会滑走，而你总是知道。其余的你也知道：我母亲，湖，什么会变得太吵。”她皱起眉，就像对着一个未来。“以前从没人把我留在今天。我想让你拿着这个数。”
# en: A seer at the lakeshore in the afternoon holding out a small hand-stitched calendar, dozens of its days marked with the same tiny drawn star.
scene [6f7650] = 午后的湖岸，一位先知递出一本手缝的小日历，几十个日子上都画着同样一颗小星星。
# en: Promise to keep counting
opt.left.label [9bc895] = 答应继续数下去
# en: "Forty-two," you say, because it's today and she's here. She laughs, a real one, finished. For the rest of the afternoon she doesn't slip once, and when you part she says "see you tomorrow", and means tomorrow.
opt.left.say.1 [45fb07] = “四十二，”你说，因为今天就是今天，而她就在这里。她笑了，一个真正的、完整的笑。那个下午她一次也没有滑走，分别时她说“明天见”，指的就是明天。
# en: Teach her a trick to find today herself
opt.right.label [ab0ccd] = 教她自己找到今天的诀窍
# en: You teach her to count the bells: the castle rings the day in a pattern, if you listen. She practises all afternoon, half a sentence at a time. The next week she slips, and finds her own way back, and comes to tell you, exact and pleased.
opt.right.say.1 [dca9ea] = 你教她数钟声：城堡每天敲钟的方式不一样，只要你听。她练了一下午，每次半句话。下个星期她又滑走了，却自己找回了路，跑来告诉你，精确而得意。

@event picture_mir
# en: Documented
title [6cb365] = 已记录
# en: Mir holds out a notebook, the newest one, open at a page with your name at the top. "I've been documenting you," they say. "Fair's fair. You know about the owl and the family and the name day and the fires. Probably all the fires. So I've been writing down what I know about you, to see if it's even." They look worried. "It isn't even. You're winning."
text [5e582b] = 米尔递过来一本笔记本，最新的那本，翻开的那页最上面写着你的名字。“我一直在记录你，”TA 说，“这才公平。你知道猫头鹰、家里、命名日和那些火灾的事。大概所有的火灾。所以我把我知道的关于你的事都写下来，看看是不是扯平了。”TA 显得很担心。“没扯平。你领先。”
# en: A cluttered workshop at night, an artificer holding out a battered notebook open at a page with someone's name at the top.
scene [2e264b] = 入夜后杂乱的工坊里，一位奇械师递出一本破旧的笔记本，翻开的那页最上面写着某人的名字。
# en: Help them fill in the page
opt.left.label [9c56ba] = 帮 TA 把这页填满
# en: You sit on the bench and answer every question, fast, the way they ask them, with exclamation marks. It takes until midnight. When it's done they read it through twice and say "huh", which from Mir means something has been mended. They file it with the precious ones.
opt.left.say.1 [8d2752] = 你坐在工作台上回答每一个问题，又快又急，就像 TA 提问那样，带着感叹号。一直弄到午夜。写完后 TA 从头读了两遍，说了声“嗯”，这在米尔那里意味着有什么东西修好了。TA 把它和那些最珍贵的放在了一起。
# en: Tell them it doesn't have to be even
opt.right.label [d37847] = 告诉 TA 不必扯平
# en: "It doesn't have to be even," you say. Mir thinks about it, visibly, like a machine running a sum. "That's very inefficient," they say. "I like it." They close the notebook. The owl on the shelf blinks twice, which is how it says "noted".
opt.right.say.1 [5ee632] = “不必扯平的，”你说。米尔想了想，看得出来，就像一台机器在算一道题。“这效率很低，”TA 说，“我喜欢。”TA 合上了笔记本。架子上的猫头鹰眨了两下眼睛，那是它说“已记下”的方式。

@event picture_bram
# en: Don't Make It Weird
title [4ae597] = 别弄得那么奇怪
# en: You find Bram in the corridor of head boys, in front of his father's portrait. He doesn't move when you come up. "You know all of it," he says, to the portrait. "The exam. The hall tax. Him. Every rematch." He clears his throat. "Most people know the sash. You know the rest, and you never once used it." He's very red. "Don't make it weird."
text [5f3f3a] = 你在历届男生学生会主席的画像走廊里找到了布拉姆，他站在他父亲的画像前。你走过来时他没动。“你全都知道，”他对着画像说，“那场考试。走廊税。他。每一次重赛。”他清了清嗓子。“大多数人只知道这条绶带。你知道其余的，却从没拿来用过一次。”他脸涨得通红。“别弄得那么奇怪。”
# en: A corridor of old portraits of head boys, a prefect in a red sash standing in front of one of them with a student beside him.
scene [ddb9c2] = 一条挂满历届男生学生会主席旧画像的走廊，一位系着红绶带的级长站在其中一幅前，身旁站着一个学生。
# en: Make it a little weird
opt.left.label [07cc14] = 弄得稍微奇怪一点
# en: You put your arm round his shoulders and tell the portrait, firmly, that its son is going to be a better prefect than it ever was. Bram makes a noise like a kettle. Then he laughs, really laughs, and gives you a demerit for "insolence to a painting".
opt.left.say.1 [ab34c4] = 你搂住他的肩膀，郑重地告诉那幅画像，它的儿子会成为一个比它当年好得多的级长。布拉姆发出一声像水壶一样的声音。然后他笑了，真正地笑了，给你记了一笔“对画作无礼”。
# en: Stand there with him, and don't
opt.right.label [12cc60] = 陪他站着，什么也不做
# en: You stand there with him and say nothing at all, which is the kindest thing you've ever done for him. After a while he says "right" and walks off, briskly. The next day there's a note in your bag in block capitals: THANK YOU. DON'T.
opt.right.say.1 [56b995] = 你陪他站在那儿，一句话也没说，这是你为他做过的最温柔的事。过了一会儿，他说了声“好吧”，快步走开了。第二天你的书包里有一张用大写字母写的字条：谢谢。别。

@event picture_maud
# en: Over Tea, Dearie
title [8347d7] = 喝杯茶吧，亲爱的
# en: Maud pours two cups and doesn't sit. "You know about Edmund," she says. "And the garden, and Tuppence, and my knees, and the soup. You've heard all my sad stories, dearie, and you've never once looked sorry for me." She sits, finally. "Sixty years since anyone knew me all the way through. I'd forgotten what it was like."
text [ea92d6] = 莫德倒了两杯茶，却没坐下。“你知道埃德蒙的事，”她说，“还有那座花园，还有塔彭丝，还有我的膝盖，还有汤。我那些伤心事你全听过了，亲爱的，可你从没露出过一次可怜我的样子。”她终于坐下了。“六十年来，再没人这样从里到外地了解我。我都忘了那是什么滋味。”
# en: A cottage kitchen, a pot of soup on the stove, an old woman pouring two cups of tea at a scrubbed table, a goat looking in at the window.
scene [f0df80] = 小屋的厨房里，炉子上炖着一锅汤，一位老妇人在擦洗干净的桌边倒两杯茶，一只山羊从窗外往里看。
# en: Ask her to teach you the soup
opt.left.label [250e0e] = 请她教你做那锅汤
# en: "You're not allowed to write it down," she says, and teaches you anyway, slowly, with her hands over yours on the spoon. You understand, two weeks later, that she wasn't teaching you the soup at all.
opt.left.say.1 [41c58f] = “不许写下来，”她说，还是教了你，慢慢地，她的手覆在你握勺的手上。两个星期后你才明白，她教你的根本不是汤。
# en: Tell her a sad story of yours
opt.right.label [f5bc7c] = 给她讲一件你的伤心事
# en: You tell her one, as if it were a recipe. She listens, and nods, and at the end says, "Needs salt." It's exactly right. Bartholomew bleats at the window. She gives him a biscuit, and you another.
opt.right.say.1 [5fef2b] = 你讲了一件，像讲一道菜谱。她听着，点着头，最后说：“得加点盐。”说得一点没错。巴塞洛缪在窗外咩咩叫。她给了它一块饼干，又给了你一块。

@event picture_thorne
# en: Hm
title [eb3e6e] = 嗯
# en: You hold the basket while Thorne cuts roses at dawn, and his hands shake, and he lets you see them shake. "You know about the storm," he says. "The real version. And the roses. And these." He holds up his hands. "And the old fool in purple." A long pause. "Hm." From Thorne, it's a speech.
text [8a75c7] = 黎明时，索恩剪玫瑰，你替他提着篮子，他的手在抖，而他让你看见了。“你知道那场风暴的事，”他说，“真正的版本。还有玫瑰。还有这个。”他举起双手。“还有那个穿紫衣服的老傻瓜。”长长的停顿。“嗯。”从索恩嘴里说出来，这就是一篇演讲。
# en: A tiny walled rose garden behind an observatory at dawn, an old professor with secateurs, his hands not quite steady, a student holding the basket.
scene [26481e] = 观星台后面一座小小的围墙玫瑰园，黎明时分，一位老教授拿着修枝剪，手不太稳，一个学生提着篮子。
# en: Ask him to tell you about the storm again
opt.left.label [1a6fd8] = 请他再讲讲那场风暴
# en: He tells you, the whole of it, the way he never tells it in lectures: how badly he lost, and how. At the end he hands you the secateurs. "Your turn," he says, meaning the roses, meaning more than the roses. "Badly is fine. Badly is the point."
opt.left.say.1 [af6a4a] = 他讲了，从头到尾，用一种他在课上从不讲的方式：他输得有多惨，又是怎么输的。最后他把修枝剪递给你。“轮到你了，”他说，指的是玫瑰，又不只是玫瑰。“输得惨没关系。输得惨才是重点。”
# en: Say nothing, and cut the next rose for him
opt.right.label [384a48] = 什么也不说，替他剪下一朵
# en: You take the secateurs and cut the next rose, carefully, and the one after that. He watches, and doesn't correct you, which has never happened. At the end he says nothing at all, and doesn't take the secateurs back. You'll be proud of that for years.
opt.right.say.1 [618145] = 你接过修枝剪，小心地剪下一朵，又剪下一朵。他看着，没有纠正你，这是从来没有过的事。最后他什么也没说，也没把修枝剪要回去。这会让你骄傲好多年。

@event picture_brask
# en: Half a Sentence More
title [1ef755] = 多说半句
# en: In the loft, Brask feeds the old owl and, for once, talks to you in a whole sentence. "You know about the owl, and the feather, and the woman with the blackthorn, and that I bow to the wood." She feeds the owl another mouse. "Students don't usually stay long enough to learn that much. The owl's noticed. So have I."
text [6b848b] = 在阁楼上，布拉斯克一边喂那只老猫头鹰，一边破天荒地对你说了一句完整的话。“你知道猫头鹰的事，还有那根羽毛，还有那个砍黑刺李的女人，还有我向林子鞠躬。”她又喂了猫头鹰一只老鼠。“学生通常待不了那么久，学不到那么多。猫头鹰注意到了。我也注意到了。”
# en: A stable loft at dusk, an old barn owl on a beam, a professor in a leather apron sitting on a hay bale beside a student.
scene [cc1991] = 黄昏时的马厩阁楼，一只老仓鸮蹲在横梁上，一位系着皮围裙的教授和一个学生并排坐在干草捆上。
# en: Ask her which loss hurt most
opt.left.label [0b9c27] = 问她哪一次失去最痛
# en: She's quiet for a long time. Then she tells you, in a whole sentence, then another, and you understand why she never would before. At the end the owl hoots once, softly, as if it had been waiting. "There," she says. "That's the moral."
opt.left.say.1 [a95e84] = 她沉默了很久。然后她告诉了你，用一句完整的话，又一句，你明白了她以前为什么从不肯说。最后，猫头鹰轻轻叫了一声，仿佛一直在等。“好了，”她说，“这就是寓意。”
# en: Ask the owl instead
opt.right.label [c6ca6d] = 改问猫头鹰
# en: You turn to the owl and ask it, very politely, what it thinks of you. The owl regards you with contempt. Brask laughs, loudly, the once-a-term laugh, a month early. "It likes you," she says. "That's its liking face."
opt.right.say.1 [5bfd52] = 你转向猫头鹰，非常礼貌地问它对你有什么看法。猫头鹰轻蔑地打量着你。布拉斯克大笑起来，那一学期一次的大笑，提前了一个月。“它喜欢你，”她说，“这就是它喜欢人的表情。”
